 ♣J ♣Q ♠K ♥K ♥A ♦A ♦2 — a relatively balanced hand with potential for sequences or pairs later.\n\nThere is no alternative move that beats the landlord’s play except the bomb. Passing keeps me safe but cedes initiative completely.\n\nReason: I must play aggressively here because my teammate did not support, and allowing the landlord to win this trick unchallenged risks accelerating their path to winning the round. Playing the bomb is the only way to contest it, and given the landlord’s long lead, disruption is critical. As a peasant, taking control now may create space for my teammate to follow suit later.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠5", "♥5", "♣5", "♦5"]}'}
